Patch to flutter_litert 3.9.3 (https://pub.dev/packages/flutter_litert), applied by
tool/flutter_litert/vendor.sh into third_party/flutter_litert. flutter_litert, and this patch as
a modification of it, stay under flutter_litert's own licence, the Apache License 2.0
(third_party/flutter_litert/LICENSE after vendoring); this app's Apache-2.0 LICENSE at the
repository root does not replace it. Changed files: lib/src/bindings/litert_ffi.dart,
linux/CMakeLists.txt (why: see the comments the patch adds).

--- a/lib/src/bindings/litert_ffi.dart
+++ b/lib/src/bindings/litert_ffi.dart
@@ -96,6 +96,18 @@
 
 typedef LiteRtOpaquePayloadDeleterNative = Void Function(Pointer<Void>);
 
+/// Whether [dylib] takes an environment as the first model-loading argument.
+/// `LiteRtCreateModelFromFd` is absent from the 2.1.5 dylib and present in the
+/// newer runtimes (LiteRT-LM's libLiteRt.so on Linux), so on desktop its
+/// presence identifies the newer ABI. Not on iOS: the runtime this plugin
+/// loads there (`litert-ios-v1.0.1`) exports it, yet its model loaders take
+/// no environment (`LiteRtCreateModelFromBuffer(buffer, size, model)`), and
+/// passing one first fails every model with
+/// kLiteRtStatusErrorInvalidFlatbuffer.
+bool _hasEnvironmentModelAbi(DynamicLibrary dylib) =>
+    Platform.isAndroid ||
+    (!Platform.isIOS && dylib.providesSymbol('LiteRtCreateModelFromFd'));
+
 int Function(Pointer<Void>, Pointer<Utf8>, Pointer<Pointer<Void>>)
